<lines>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_1">##SECTIO I.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_2">#Quot sint pretia rerum</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_3">#vendibilium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_4">##SVMMARIVM.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_5">>>>1 Res, quae venditur, &amp; pretium eius</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_6">>>sunt materia venditionis.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_7">>>>2 Pretium latissimè sumitur pro cuius¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_8">>>cumque rei [-aestimatione] aestimatione.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_9">>>>3 Aestimatio est iudicium quo rem cū</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_10">>>alijs conferendo alijs praeferimus,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_11">>>alijs postponimus, alijs coaequa¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_12">>>mus.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_13">>>>4 Aestimatio Dei semper [-est]est [-iusta]iusta, ho¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_14">>>minum autem mendax, &amp; fallax</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_15">>>saepissimè.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_16">>>>5 Rectus rerum [-aestimator]aestimator iustus [-est]est,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_17">>>&amp; sanctus.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_18">>>>6 Strictè pretium est pecunia, quia est</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_19">>>mensura rerum venalium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_20">>>>7 Pretium triplex legale, naturale, cō¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_21">>>uentionale.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_22">>>>8 Explicatur trimembris diuisio.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_23">>>Pretium legale quid?</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_24">>>>9 In indiuisibili [=conſistit]consistit</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_25">>>>10 In quo sensu consistat in indiuisibili.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_26">>>>11 Per quos fiat pretium legale.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_27">>>>12 Pretium naturale, siue vulgare</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_28">>>quid.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_29">>>>13 Habet latitudinem rigorosi, medio¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_30">>>cris, &amp; pij.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_31">>>>14 Siue supremi, medij, &amp; infimi.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_32">>>>15 Dicitur naturale, quia nullius arbi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_33">>>trio subiacet, sed omnium colle¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_34">>>ctiuè.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_35">>>>16 Tres secuelae ex hoc in praxi valde</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_36">>>vtiles.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_37">>>>17 Pretium conuentionale quia.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_38">>>>18 Conuentione contrahētium pretium</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_39">>>hoc conuentionale [-constituitur]constituitur.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_40">>>>19 Magis habet de arbitrio, &amp; latitudi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_41">>>ne, quam alia hoc conuentionale</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_42">>>pretium.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_43">>>>20 An possint contrahentes in minus, &amp;</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_44">>>maius pretium conuenire.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_45">>>>21 Primò vsurpatur pretium legale,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_46">>>secundò naturale, tertiò conuen¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_47">>>tionale.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_48">>>>23 An lege conuentionale habeat infini¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_49">>>tam latitudinem.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_50">>>>24 Probatur quinque argumentis pars</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_51">>>affirmans.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_52">>>>25 Huiusce opinionis DD.</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_53">>>>26 Resoluitur conuentionale etiam limi¬</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_54">>>tes suos habere, sed valde laxos,</line>
  <line id="tr_1_tl_56">>>&amp; amplissimos.</line>
</lines>
